  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Respond to the challenges of human mobility in Honduras by providing assistance and protection to people in mixed movements.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this UNHCR project is to improve the protection environment and services for people in mixed movements. The project aims at improving the reception conditions and response capacities for people in need, by providing life-saving information and orientation, psychological and medical services, in addition to shelter to vulnerable population in mixed movements. The intervention provides humanitarian assistance to 15,000 people (7,200 men, 4,050 women and 3,750 children), including 450 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
